## Context
DESIGN.md §2.6 defers #6012-style calibration (mean centering, noise floor =
p99 of unrelated pairs, display ceiling = median of matched pairs, reject a
model whose matched-median <= null-p99) "to its own ticket with a stated
pair-generation protocol" — this is that ticket. Protocol: matched pairs =
title<->abstract of one item; unrelated pairs = cross-item; the library is the
corpus. Until built, frac_vec defaults to list-local max-normalization.
Deferred: only worth building if fraction-RRF ships (the query-semantics work
riding scoped issue A, 0033 — formerly 0023's PR-12) and the golden gate shows
the default normalization losing.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] calibration block computed per model-version from library-derived pairs
- [ ] model-rejection rule enforced ("better to fail loudly than index with it")
- [ ] frac_vec uses the calibrated floor/ceiling; golden set shows no regression
